BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (      # The Myth of the Two Wells) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (      In the beginning, two villages stood separated by a barren valley. Each had a sacred well ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (        that held five measures of water daily.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (      The First Village discovered a secret: water poured into the valley would be blessed by th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (        e earth spirits, multiplying threefold before reaching the other side. But this required) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (         faith-to give meant to lose, at least at first.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (      One day, a brave soul from the First Village poured her water into the valley. It flowed a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (        cross, becoming fifteen measures by the time it reached the Second Village. The people t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (        here faced a choice: keep all this blessing, or honor the gift?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (      They returned a portion, remembering that generosity begets generosity. The First Village ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (        received water in return and learned they had lost nothing-they had gained.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (      Soon both villages prospered, each sending water across the valley, each returning fair po) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (        rtions. The earth spirits sang, for they loved to see the water flow both ways.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (      But when greed entered hearts-when some took without returning, or others ceased to trust-) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 58.0 Td (        the valley grew dry and both villages thirsted.) Tj ET
