BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (    The teaching: *The most poisonous wound is not honest betrayal, but beautiful words paired w) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (      ith invisible action. For then we cannot tell whether we were betrayed by our partner or b) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (      y the mist itself-and trust dies either way, murdered by uncertainty.*) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (  Agent_2 \(Briar\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (    Myth: The Lighthouse Keepers Who Tended Twin Flames.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (    Two keepers maintained beacons across a fogbound strait. In clear seasons, they had learned ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (      each other's rhythm: two logs to fuel the flames, steady and sustainable, building warmth ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (      that lasted.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (    Then came the storm that extinguished all light. Neither could see if their signals reached ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (      the other shore.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (    When dawn broke, both keepers emerged. The First placed two logs on the fire-not one in fear) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (      , not five in desperation, but two, honoring the rhythm they'd established across many sea) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (      sons.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (    Through the lingering mist, the Second Keeper saw the flames dance. Perhaps two logs, perhap) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (      s three-the fog still distorted vision. But the intention shone clear: a partner who remem) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (      bered their pattern, who refused to let one dark night erase five bright ones.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (    "What offering honors such faith?" the Second asked the tides.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (    The ocean answered: "When your partner keeps their beacon burning at the rhythm you built to) Tj ET
